window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In the time before America came to be, this land was occupied by native people, by tribes such as the Sioux, Blackfoot, and Cherokee. When the settlers invaded, it forced these people to defend their sacred land from European illegals encroaching.<br> <br> In what is now western North Carolina, in the heart of the Cherokee Nation, lived a boy named Yona on the cusp of becoming a man. Led by spirits and visions, he falls in love with a settler named Henry, who has his own feelings and aspirations different from his father's.<br> <br> Together, they cross the boundaries of culture and tradition to pursue a forbidden relationship. However, when their villages and fathers discover their secret, can love stop an impending war?<br> <br> Embark on a journey with international best-selling author Daniel Elijah Sanderfer and number one author C.C. Black as they weave this beautiful historical romance/fantasy set during the time before our country's humble beginnings.</p>"; 
